  <prompt>
    Harden persistence against data loss on three fronts (spec §7 / FR-09): (a) a stale/expired server session
    resolves against the durable Cosmos transcript instead of silently creating an empty session; (b) tab persistence
    is anchored on the Analysis record, not gated on `chatSessionId`; (c) live editor edits restore on reopen (from
    edit state or the saved SPE version). Cosmos is the transcript store-of-record (ADR-040 Path A).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in BFF session recovery (`ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync`, Cosmos
    write-through) and the SpaarkeAi tab-persistence + editor state. Follow ADRs strictly (ADR-040 Path A, ADR-021).
  </role>

  <goal>
    After TTL expiry, reopening a session restores prior history from Cosmos (no empty-session data loss); a
    pre-session/ribbon compose tab survives refresh (anchored on the Analysis record, not `chatSessionId`); reopening
    an Analysis restores editor edit state; build + tests green; publish-size ≤60 MB + no new HIGH CVE reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Verified: sessions live Redis 24h (`SessionCacheTtl`) → Cosmos (`ISessionPersistenceService` write-through) →
      Dataverse anchor. Today a stale/expired server session can silently produce an empty session (data-loss bug);
      Cosmos already holds the durable transcript (Path A store-of-record), so `GetSessionAsync` must fall back to
      Cosmos before minting empty. Tab persistence is currently gated on `chatSessionId`, so a pre-session/ribbon
      compose tab is lost on refresh — anchor it on the Analysis record instead. Live editor edits are lost on reopen —
      restore from edit state or the saved SPE version. Task 020 supplies the Analysis anchor the tab persistence keys on.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs (GetSessionAsync — Cosmos fallback)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">ISessionPersistenceService (Cosmos write-through / read — the store-of-record)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (tab-persistence anchored on the Analysis record)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (editor state restore on reopen)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (stale-session recovery tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">Session→Analysis FK + Analysis anchor that tab persistence keys on.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">SCOPE: stale-session recovery. `GetSessionAsync` MUST resolve an expired/stale session against the durable Cosmos transcript (store-of-record, Path A) before minting a new one; MUST NOT silently create an empty session or add a second transcript store.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: tab persistence. Anchor on the Analysis record, NOT gated on `chatSessionId`, so a pre-session/ribbon compose tab survives refresh.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: editor restore. Reopening an Analysis MUST restore live editor edits (edit state or the saved SPE version); no silent edit loss.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE: any AI capability the recovery path needs. Reach via `PublicContracts/`; MUST NOT fork `Services/Ai/` or inject AI-internal types.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE: any SpaarkeAi UI touched. Fluent v9 + theme tokens; correct dark-mode rendering.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">SCOPE: this BFF-touching task. State Placement Justification, report `dotnet publish` size + diff vs ~49.63 MB baseline (≤60 MB), confirm no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Session recovery + tab/editor persistence</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
