      <file>.claude/patterns/ai/public-contracts-facade.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-component-authoring.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Cosmos store-of-record" location="ISessionPersistenceService">
        Resolve a stale session by reading the durable Cosmos transcript before minting; Cosmos is the Path A store-of-record.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor + reason; load knowledge; reproduce the silent empty-session case in `GetSessionAsync`.</step>
    <step order="1">(a) Add the Cosmos fallback in `GetSessionAsync`: on stale/expired Redis session, read the durable Cosmos transcript and rehydrate rather than minting empty.</step>
    <step order="2">(b) Re-anchor SpaarkeAi tab persistence on the Analysis record (not `chatSessionId`) so a pre-session/ribbon compose tab survives refresh.</step>
    <step order="3">(c) Restore live editor edits on reopen (from edit state or the saved SPE version).</step>
    <step order="4">Add BFF tests for stale-session recovery (TTL-expiry reopen restores history, no empty session); client checks for tab-survives-refresh + editor-restore.</step>
    <step order="5">`/conflict-check` vs redesign-r1/r2; `dotnet build` + `dotnet test`; `dotnet publish` size + CVE report.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set 025 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a stale session cannot be resolved against Cosmos (e.g. the transcript is genuinely absent, not just Redis-expired), STOP before minting a silent empty session and escalate for the correct no-data-loss behavior (CLAUDE.md §6) rather than discarding history.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="TTL-expiry reopen restores history">
      <steps><step>Create a session with messages; expire it past `SessionCacheTtl`.</step><step>Reopen the Analysis.</step></steps>
      <expected>Prior history is restored from Cosmos; no empty-session data loss.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Compose tab survives refresh">
      <steps><step>Open a pre-session/ribbon compose tab; refresh the page.</step></steps>
      <expected>The tab survives (anchored on the Analysis record, not gated on `chatSessionId`); renders correctly in dark mode (ADR-021).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Editor edits restore on reopen">
      <steps><step>Make live edits in the editor; close + reopen the Analysis.</step></steps>
      <expected>Edit state (or the saved SPE version) is restored; no silent edit loss.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test BFF; `dotnet publish -c Release`; `dotnet list package --vulnerable`.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build the SpaarkeAi client.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/ChatSessionManager.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/ (tab-persistence + editor restore)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (stale-session recovery tests)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a session past TTL expiry, when reopened, then prior history is restored from the Cosmos transcript with no empty-session data loss.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a pre-session/ribbon compose tab, when the page is refreshed, then the tab survives (anchored on the Analysis record, not `chatSessionId`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given live editor edits, when the Analysis is closed and reopened, then edit state (or the saved SPE version) is restored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `GetSessionAsync` does NOT silently create an empty session when a durable Cosmos transcript exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SpaarkeAi UI touched renders correctly in light + dark mode (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish-size ≤60 MB compressed (diff reported); no new HIGH CVE; all unit tests pass; build green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-09 / §7 / PLAN §2.6 / NFR-04 (no session/transcript data loss). Cosmos is the durable store-of-record
    (ADR-040 Path A). `/conflict-check` before the BFF PR.

    COMPLETED 2026-07-29. This task was implemented by a prior (interrupted) agent run; this pass was a
    verify-and-finalize (task-execute Step 9.5 completion), NOT a re-implementation. No code changes were
    necessary — the on-disk diff was coherent, reuse-first, and defect-free.

    Summary of implementation verified: (a) `ChatSessionManager.GetSessionAsync` wraps the Cosmos
    `LoadSessionAsync` warm-path read in a try/catch — a transient Cosmos failure now logs a warning and
    degrades to the existing Dataverse cold path instead of throwing (which a caller could otherwise
    misread as "not found" and mint an empty session over a still-durable transcript). No new store was
    created; the existing Redis→Cosmos→Dataverse cascade is unchanged in shape. (b) SpaarkeAi tab
    persistence in `WorkspacePane.tsx` gained a `tabAnchorKeyForContext()`-derived localStorage cache keyed
    on the bound Analysis record (`entityType:entityId`), written on every debounced persist tick and read
    as a fallback when there is no `chatSessionId` yet or the BFF returns 404 for the session's tabs — this
    is what makes a pre-session/ribbon-compose tab survive a refresh. Reuses the SAME localStorage-with-
    try/catch convention already established elsewhere in this codebase (`chipPreference.ts`,
    `SemanticSearchCriteriaTool.tsx`, `ManageWorkspacesPane.tsx` pane-collapse) — not a new persistence
    mechanism; the BFF PATCH/GET path remains the durable cross-device store once a session exists.
    `WorkspaceTabManager.updateTab` now fires `_notifyPersistChange()` (the one mutating method that
    previously didn't) plus a stale-tab-id guard. (c) `AnalysisEditorWidget` gained `onDataChange` /
    `data.isEditing` + `data.draftSections` restore hints, threaded through
    `WorkspaceWidgetWrapper`/`widget-types.ts` (optional prop, forwarded verbatim) and
    `WorkspaceTabManagerComponent`'s `onTabDataChange` → `WorkspacePane.handleTabDataChange` (merges the
    patch onto the tab's `widgetData` and calls `updateTab`, riding the same write-through as (b)) — a
    live, unsaved edit now survives tab close/reopen or page refresh; Save/Cancel clear the restore hints
    so no stale draft haunts a later reopen.

    Gates run this pass:
    - code-review: 0 Critical. 2 Warning (both pre-existing-pattern-adjacent, not defects): (1) the new
      `sprk_ai2_workspaceTabs__{type}:{id}` localStorage key namespace has no eviction/cap, unlike the
      sibling `chipPreference.ts` pattern that caps its tracked set — could grow one entry per Analysis
      ever opened over a long-lived browser profile (low practical risk; small JSON payloads, try/catch
      wrapped for quota errors); (2) `AnalysisEditorWidget`'s per-keystroke `onDataChange` triggers
      `WorkspacePane.syncState()` (an undebounced `setTabState`) on every keystroke while editing, though
      the actual write-through (localStorage + BFF PATCH) IS already debounced 200ms — a possible
      per-keystroke re-render, likely negligible given typical section-edit cardinality. Neither blocks
      merge; both are candidates for a follow-up task if profiling shows real impact. No fix applied (no
      Critical found).
    - adr-check: 0 violations across ADR-040 (no second transcript store; try/catch degrades to the
      existing cold path, does not silently mint empty — verified by the negative-criterion test below),
      ADR-013 (no new CRUD→AI-internal injection; change is internal to an existing session-recovery
      method), ADR-021 (no styling/color changes; AnalysisEditorWidget's existing Fluent v9 dark-mode
      tests untouched and still passing), ADR-028 (no auth surface touched), ADR-012 (additive optional
      prop threading through existing wrapper forwarding, not a new component).
    - Negative acceptance criterion verified: `GetSessionAsync_StaleSessionPastTtl_CosmosHasTranscript_
      RestoresHistory_NoEmptySessionDataLoss` asserts 2 prior messages are restored (not an empty session)
      and Dataverse is never consulted; `GetSessionAsync_CosmosReadThrows_FallsBackToDataverse_DoesNotThrow`
      covers the transient-failure path. Both pass.
    - BFF tests: `ChatSessionManagerTests` 23/23 passed. Full unit suite: 9029 passed / 8 failed / 101
      skipped — the 8 failures (3 `AnalysisEndpointsExecuteDispatchContractTests`, 5
      `Services/Communication/*`) were reproduced identically with the task-025 diff `git stash`'d out,
      confirming pre-existing and unrelated (same 8 as task 023's baseline).
    - Client: `npm run typecheck` (SpaarkeAi) — `tsc-surface-gate`: 244 pre-existing shared-lib errors
      (deferred to Phase B), 0 surface-owned. `WorkspaceTabManager.test.ts`: 67/67 passed (incl. the 2 new
      `updateTab`/`onPersistChange` tests). `AnalysisEditorWidget.test.tsx`: 12/12 passed (incl. the 5 new
      restore/persist tests).
    - Publish-size: `dotnet publish -c Release` → 46.16 MB compressed (`Compress-Archive`, matching the
      task-023 measurement methodology) vs the 47.52 MB baseline recorded in task 023's notes — a **-1.36
      MB** delta (net decrease; well under the +5 MB single-task justification threshold and the 55/60 MB
      ceilings). `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: only the pre-existing
      `System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 8.0.3` HIGH advisories (zero package changes this task).
    - Build: `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` green (0 errors, pre-existing warnings only,
      already confirmed before this verification pass).
  </notes>

